  "implementation": [
    "Replace initial-only consultation/return outsider selection with purpose-bound SipAudienceOrigin/SipAudienceRead variants for actual initial and committed SIP lifetimes. Current complete scene discovery includes both kinds; duplicate, omitted, retired, foreign Session and overlapping native/physical IDs refuse rather than silently reducing the audience.",
    "Committed outsider metadata records its real generation/call/route owner and current Endpoint/Device. It has no initial endpoint credential or native signing projection. Both variants acquire their own current media reads under the merged audience interval. These reads cannot supply a private native slot.",
    "Consultation and return carry the exact SIP controller/principal and original audience receipt, including actual committed target control and typed source edges on return. The retired replacement preparation reader is not reused. Native source and Participant callbacks retain separate actual physical checks.",
    "Captured audience metadata dispatches by actual SIP source kind. Established revision updates require the exact original confirmed lifetime, live generation, runtime, call, original revision and next revision. Recording cannot revive a retired route or rewrite a newer observation. Store schema and upstream sources remain unchanged.",
    "Generated HTTP/OpenAPI reference and developer guide describe the outside-only scope. Captured private-input validator accepts explicit initial or established source profiles and verifies the moved source identity and zero marked private audio at the outside SIP socket."
  ],
