  "actual_behavior": [
    "Public movement to the configured SIP account, revocation of original source/controller credentials and expiry of original preparation precede the composed profile. A fresh real Session-manager native control credential invites new participants without replacing or authorizing the SIP route.",
    "The new private pair uses the actual native primary and independently signed consultant, with a separate retained native remote. Its complete outside selection contains exactly the actual committed SIP generation2/record/call. A public Device of the consultant shares the logical Participant while retaining its independent physical Connection.",
    "Baseline actual SIP INFO delivers two signed frames. Private activation proves decoded native audio in both private directions; the outside moved SIP socket receives zero marked private audio for either source after draining prior public packets.",
    "Actual SIP INFO during the private scene is delivered only to the authorized public sibling. Store excludes the privately admitted candidate. The original public primary remains frozen metadata but the current Core audience refuses physical receipt, preserving its truthful NotStarted disposition. The operation reports partial submission rather than hiding the refused recipient.",
    "Pending reliable readers span quiet absence, actual public return, retransmission of the old INFO and fresh negotiated RFC4733 input. Return retires only the private candidate and preserves the retained remote. Replay never gains the returned primary or a new audience. Fresh input reaches the primary and public sibling with two new exact frame IDs, while the retired candidate receives no signal.",
    "Across EdDSA and ES256, ten actual signed frames and six source-owner HTTP summaries validate full frozen wire/status schemas, original physical source kind/time, digits5 and237ms duration. The SDK verifies signatures. Old partial HTTP status remains byte-equivalent on replay; source row count remains exactly3 per scene and the single configured dialog closes with owned server/listener cleanup.",
    "Four installed production regressions pass: initial SIP outside private pair with return, ordinary moved received input/current authority/media denial, moved DTMF credential refresh, and disjoint all-native private groups returning independently. The102 selected Store methods include the three new committed outsider tests, initial SIP source, private provider source, consultation planning/attempt/lifetime/return and credential-refresh custody cases."
  ],
  "intermediate_checks": [
    "The first Store build rejected private methods in the new child module; restricted them to pub(super) and reran the three new tests successfully. The selected102-method regression run passes.",
    "The first default build reported initial Leg::owner visibility when used by typed audience dispatch. Exposed only this existing helper within the service crate. The corrected service/MCP/server/test build passes. An ignored compiler sample confirms active MIR validation during the long public-type rebuild; it was allowed to finish.",
    "The first physical test correctly refused a non-manager existing-Session invitation at the fixture helper. Used a fresh actual native credential for the original Session manager, whose old credential was already revoked. No production authorization rule was weakened. The corrected test-only rebuild and both final signing scenes pass.",
    "Existing upstream private-interface and macOS linker unwind-size warnings remain in ignored logs. The separate validator regression rechecks the historical initial-SIP capture shape; current initial-SIP runtime behavior is independently rerun in the four-production-method regression set."
  ],
